  <!-- Column 2 Text -->
  <div slot="col-2-text">
    <p>
      It’s the last month of the year<br>
      What does it mean to you;<br>
      Not enough hours in the day<br>
      For the things you have to do.<br>
      Cakes to bake plum pudding to make<br>
      Christmas cards and presents to buy;<br>
      Stretching beyond financial means<br>
      No matter how hard you may try.<br>
      After a massive long tiring trip<br>
      You struggle on home exhausted;<br>
      Now all the things you bought await<br>
      To be written, wrapped and posted.<br>
      No time left for newsy letters<br>
      Festive greetings will have to do;<br>
      Will another full year pass by<br>
      E’er they hear again from you?<br>
      Getting cards and expensive gifts<br>
      May be lovely to behold;<br>
      But newsy letters from the heart<br>
      To friends -- are richer than gold.<br>
      Forget the trimmings and relax<br>
      Recall the good times you are given;<br>
      Share memories with those you love<br>
      Of blessings sent down from Heaven.<br>
      December Celebrations<br>
      By Eila Webster
    </p>
  </div>

